test ops::bootstrap::tests::test_verified_modswitch_validates_residues ... ignored, RETIRED MECHANISM: literally asserts mod-switch validation succeeds — assert!(result.is_ok(), "Valid ciphertext should pass K-Elimination validation") on boot.modswitch_to_t_verified(&ct, &ke). The thing being validated is the rounded divide-and-drop-the-basis step, which this substrate does not perform: exact division in residue space divides the value without moving the basis, so no level is consumed and there is no switch whose residues need validating. K-Elimination itself is NOT retired — it is the exact-division primitive; only its use as a guard on a modulus switch is. CAVEAT — the proximate panic is the deprecated ke.capacity() u128 overflow under KElimConfig::Extended, not the retirement. See docs/RETIRED_MECHANISMS.md
