test ops::rns_fhe::tests::test_ntt_ternary_mul ... ignored, TEST-ONLY BUG (not production): the manual reference computation (`expected_as_0`) extracts `a_coeffs[i] = ctx.rns.to_int(&a_res) as i128` directly, uncentered, then uses it as a SIGNED value in a naive negacyclic convolution -- `s_coeffs` right next to it IS properly centered. `a` (pk1) is a uniform ring element, not a small signed value, so treating its raw unsigned-mod-M residue as already-signed is only correct while `a` stays below M/2. Before G12 fixed `a`-sampling (previously confined to `[0, min_prime)`, which for this 2-prime ~60-bit `light_rns_exact_insecure` config accidentally kept it under M/2), that held by luck; the corrected uniform sampling makes it false about half the time, so this test's own naive convolution now disagrees with the correct production result. Production paths are unaffected -- see `test_tracked_multiplication`, `test_coeff_domain_full_ct_mul`, and the full fhe-service test suite, all passing.
